    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0438" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1164 University of Shanghai/61:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-09T16:00:00-04:00">August 9, 1938—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>277. Your 501, July 30, 11 a.m.,<anchor n="50" xml:id="d586-f1"/> in regard to
                    the University of Shanghai. The Department desires that at such time as you
                    consider opportune and in such manner as you deem appropriate you continue your
                    efforts to obtain a satisfactory settlement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d586-f1" n="50" xml:id="d586-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; but see the Ambassador’s memorandum of July 30, <ref
                        target="frus1931-41v01#pg_778"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, p. 778</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
